  "responseText": "{\"reviewedAffectedSlots\":[\"W043\",\"W049\",\"W054\"],\"findings\":[\"W043 (nnxyz nifty faces #21): Correctly composited over white canvas. The ground is open white, not a dark fill. The head is built from dense, overlapping colored lines — prominent red and yellow sweeps, black hatching, teal and green accents — with the white ground showing through the gaps. The two black cross marks for eyes sit inside a busy field of red loops and yellow strokes, not against a neutral or dark surround. The form tilts and is far more colorful and open than the prior description implied; calling it 'flat' and 'locked' on an 'open white ground' is partially correct but the density and color variety were underdescribed, and the crown-like top cluster of marks is a visible structural feature.\",\"W049 (nnxyz nifty faces #34): Correctly composited over white canvas. The background is white, not a tinted or dark field. The oval head is filled with vivid cyan, magenta, yellow, green, and white lines crossing in multiple directions; the white ground shows through at the lower face and chin area. The mouth is large, wide, and rimmed in deep magenta-red with visible teeth marks, not merely 'red-rimmed.' The eyes are dark, heavily outlined forms set high in the oval. The tilt of the head is pronounced. The prior description's reference to a colored background is incorrect; the surrounding field is white.\",\"W054 (nnxyz nifty faces #11): Correctly composited over white canvas. The background is white with lines extending freely to the edges. The hat is a wide-brimmed form built from the same multicolored scribble as the face — black, magenta, yellow, blue, green lines — not a distinct dark horizontal band. The face beneath is densely layered with the same spectrum of colors, eyes and nose legible through the accumulation. The white ground shows through in several areas of the hat and upper corners. The prior description's characterization of a 'dense horizontal band of crossing lines' forming the hat brim is directionally correct but understates the color variety and the continuity between hat and face marks; it also did not note the white ground.\"],\"membershipConcerns\":[],\"corrections\":[{\"slot\":\"W043\",\"whyHere\":\"The head is assembled from dense, overlapping lines — bold red sweeps, yellow strokes, black hatching, and teal accents — all on an open white ground that shows through the gaps. Two black cross marks stand in for eyes inside a field of looping red and yellow lines, giving the face a fixed quality while the surrounding marks remain restless. A crown-like cluster of short strokes at the top adds a structural note without closing the form.\",\"transitionFromPrevious\":\"nnxyz nifty faces #22's eye-like ovals are organic forms inside a shifting dark mass; nnxyz nifty faces #21 replaces that organic quality with blunt black crosses set inside a web of red and yellow lines on white, making the face's reliance on placeholder marks visible against an open ground.\"},{\"slot\":\"W049\",\"whyHere\":\"A tilted oval head fills most of the canvas against a white ground, its surface crossed by dense lines in cyan, magenta, yellow, green, and white. The mouth is wide and prominent, rimmed in deep magenta-red with teeth marks visible inside; the dark, heavily outlined eyes sit high in the oval. White shows through at the lower face and chin, keeping the form from closing entirely despite the density of crossing lines.\",\"transitionFromPrevious\":\"nnxyz nifty faces #113's face floats in open gray space with minimal marks; nnxyz nifty faces #34 fills a similarly oval territory with crossing lines in full color on a white ground, the prominent mouth and high-set eyes holding the face readable inside that density.\"},{\"slot\":\"W054\",\"whyHere\":\"A wide-brimmed hat built from the same multicolored scribble as the face — black, magenta, yellow, blue, and green lines running in every direction — sits above a densely layered portrait, both hat and face sharing the same mark language. The white ground shows through in the hat area and upper corners, keeping the accumulated lines from merging into a solid mass. Eyes and nose remain legible through the density, the portrait held together by the concentration of marks around the features rather than by any enclosing outline.\",\"transitionFromPrevious\":\"nnxyz nifty faces #41's face is held by color contrast against a warm ground; nnxyz nifty faces #11 works on white, with hat and face built from the same continuous scribble in the same color range, so the portrait's legibility depends entirely on where the marks concentrate rather than on any change in ground or tone.\"}],\"chapterCorrections\":[]}",
